  "statement": "Let $g(x)=\\\\ln(x+\\\\sqrt{x^{2}+1})$. Show that $g'(x)=\\\\tfrac{1}{\\\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}}$ and find $g''(x)$.",
  "solution": "$g'(x)=\\\\tfrac{1+\\\\tfrac{x}{\\\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}}}{x+\\\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}}=\\\\tfrac{\\\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}+x}{(x+\\\\sqrt{x^{2}+1})\\\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}}=\\\\tfrac{1}{\\\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}}$. Then $g''(x)=\\\\tfrac{d}{dx}(x^{2}+1)^{-1/2}=-\\\\tfrac12(x^{2}+1)^{-3/2}\\\\cdot2x=-\\\\tfrac{x}{(x^{2}+1)^{3/2}}$.",
